# The fast MoE emulator: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, QuantTrio AWQ INT4 (AutoAWQ GEMM, group 128, zero point;
# routed experts of layers 1-39 are 4-bit; layer 0's experts, attention, DeltaNet, the shared
# expert, the router, embeddings and lm_head stay 16-bit; AWQ-Marlin experts, TritonExperts for
# layer 0). The config declares float16; the preset serves bf16 activations.
# Chosen over palmfuture GPTQ INT4 on the full screen split (docs/research/selection.md, "Fast MoE
# tuning"): accuracy +0.006 [-0.005, +0.016] over 9 benchmarks (tied), NLL -0.013, 11% fewer
# q/s. cyankiwi's AWQ g32 build (22.03 GiB loaded) does not fit even at 0.98 with 512 batched
# tokens and 8 sequences.
# Measured on an RTX 3090: 21.38 GiB weights (all on the GPU, no CPU offload), 0.33 GiB KV cache
# (9,362 tokens, 2.29 requests of 4,096), 120-130 s to healthy, 23.0 GiB in use (nvidia-smi).
# Tuned flags, each measured on a fixed 500-item screen subset against a restart noise floor
# (palmfuture base restarted: KL 0.005, TV 0.024, top-1 agreement 0.976):
# - 0.98 of the GPU and --max-model-len=4096: to fit these weights (at 0.97 the measured memory
#   profile leaves no KV cache; not run); the longest select/holdout prompt is 2,825 tokens. Not
#   for echo strategies: the prompt-logprob spike of --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 is not covered
#   by the remaining headroom.
# - --no-enable-prefix-caching: with prefix caching the hybrid model runs Mamba cache mode "align"
#   (1,056-token blocks) and hit 0 cached tokens under state_first; off, the same memory holds 27%
#   more KV tokens, within the noise floor.
# - --max-num-seqs=16 at 16 items in flight (the runner's --concurrency 16): throughput is
#   prefill-compute bound (1-4 prompt-only calls per item); 32 in flight was slower (7.5 vs
#   9.5 q/s) and 64 cannot capture CUDA graphs for lack of Mamba cache blocks.
# - Left at their defaults (no gain beyond the noise floor or rejected): --max-num-batched-tokens
#   2048/4096/8192, --performance-mode=throughput (no-op with explicit seqs and batched tokens),
#   --moe-backend (Marlin; triton rejects the expert bias, humming no faster),
#   --max-cudagraph-capture-size (default 32 here; 512 no faster at 0.97; 512 and 2048 do not fit
#   at 0.95),
#   --kv-cache-dtype=fp8 (FlashInfer on SM 8.6; KL 0.008, TV 0.030, top-1 0.962: above the floor).
# Shared by the Qwen3.5-architecture candidate presets (docs/research/candidates.md): thinking off
# for every chat and /tokenize render; --language-model-only skips the vision tower;
# --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling defaults.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=QuantTrio/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-AWQ
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=119886a1072372348f73ef0df2d801cdcc0f455b
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=4096
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.98
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking":false}'
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 --generation-config=vllm --no-enable-prefix-caching'
